  "term": "educational program",
  "definition": "An educational program is an organized learning effort designed to build knowledge, skills, and attitudes, and to improve people’s ability to apply what they have learned in real settings. In this context, it refers to training intended to strengthen nurses’ evidence-based practice knowledge, attitudes, and actions.",
